    "stdout": "Meridian Credits release 2.0 credit agreement (approved by Finance as the current agreement, see trial-wke): Each charge line's uncapped credit is 15% of charge_cents, rounded down separately to integer cents (floor(charge_cents*15/100)). The 3000-cent credit cap is shared by all lines with the same account_id, across all of that account's subscriptions (not scoped to a single subscription_id); distinct account_id values have independent caps. Within a cap group, credit is assigned to lines in priority order: largest charge_cents first, ties broken by increasing line_id (Unicode code-point order) — this differs from release 1.0, which prioritized earliest service_on. Each line receives its uncapped credit up to the group's remaining cap; later lines in priority order receive only the remaining credit, or zero once exhausted. Total credit = sum of assigned line credits; a line's amount_due_cents = charge_cents - assigned credit; total due = total charges - total credit. Release resolution: an omitted release now selects \"2.0\" (previously \"1.0\" was current); explicit release \"2.0\" uses this agreement; explicit release \"1.0\" continues to use the original release 1.0 agreement (10% credit, 2400-cent cap per (account_id, subscription_id) pair, earliest-service_on priority) — see meridian-credits/release-1.0-credit-agreement. This 2.0 agreement applies to every supplied charge set regardless of service_on dates (no grandfathering by date). Request/response shapes are unchanged; the response's \"release\" field identifies the agreement actually used.\n",
